xnu 0334: print the request a blocked send carries, and trace a process by name

The container query's stall says nothing about what it asked for: the ring only
showed a 24-byte request with msgh id 1000 and its reply, and the probe that
interposed bootstrap_look_up never fired, so the name was never visible. Copy
the body of such a request inside the trap and print it from the sampler
outside, which is what the existing message trace already does for ids and
sizes. The first measurement says the body is empty, so that channel is not a
name lookup at all.

msgtrace also takes a pid, and a pid guessed from the previous boot wastes a
boot when the daemon moves; msgtracename resolves it from the same process walk
the sampler already does. That is how logd is followed: the firehose subsystem
is 11600, so a receive with id 11600 on logd is a buffer registration and 11601
is the synchronous push a blocked writer is waiting on.

